      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "The sine rule states:",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$a^2 = b^2 + c^2 - 2bc\\cos A$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$\\frac{a}{\\sin A} = \\frac{b}{\\sin B} = \\frac{c}{\\sin C}$" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$a \\sin B = b \\sin A + c$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "The sine rule is $\\frac{a}{\\sin A} = \\frac{b}{\\sin B} = \\frac{c}{\\sin C}$, where each side is divided by the sine of its opposite angle."
